{
  "title": "Projectile Target Challenge: Pick Angle and Speed",
  "description": "A launcher sits at the left end of a flat 70 m field with marks every 10 m. A flagged target disc sits down the field. Set the launch angle and speed, then press Launch. The ball flies along its arc and leaves a trail. When it lands, readouts show the landing distance, the miss distance and whether the shot was short or long. Your previous arc stays as a faded ghost. Hit targets at 30 m, 45 m and 18 m using no more than 10 launches.",
